OwnGit {{.Version}} macOS prototype

{{if .Signed -}}
This prototype is signed with the publisher's Developer ID, uses the hardened
runtime, and was notarized by Apple; the notarization ticket is stapled to the
disk image. It is not a public release yet: it has not been installed through
a completed native acceptance run.
{{- else -}}
This unsigned local prototype is not a public release. It has no
publisher-signed app or DMG and has not been notarized or installed through a
completed native acceptance run. An ad hoc signature added to a Mach-O file by
Apple's linker is not a publisher signature.
{{- end}}

Install
  Copy OwnGit.app to your Applications folder (or ~/Applications) with
  Finder, then open it from there. OwnGit.app does not run from the disk
  image, because the OwnGit service keeps starting the program inside it.

What opening the app does
  OwnGit.app is the OwnGit icon in the menu bar. The server itself is the
  OwnGit service, a LaunchAgent that runs {{.Helper}}
  whenever you log in. The first time you open the app it installs that
  service, starts it and opens setup in your browser. System Settings lists
  the service as OwnGit under General, Login Items & Extensions. The icon
  also opens at sign-in; turn that off in the icon's settings.

The icon
  Click the icon for the panel: whether OwnGit runs, the clone address with
  a copy button, the three latest pushes and Open dashboard. The gear opens
  this Mac's icon settings. Hide from the menu bar keeps the icon hidden,
  also after the next login; turn on OwnGit icon in the dashboard's Settings,
  run {{.Helper}} tray on, or open OwnGit.app
  again to show it. Quit the icon closes it until you open the app or log in
  again. Hiding or quitting the icon never stops OwnGit: clone and push keep
  working.

Stop
  {{.Helper}} service stop stops OwnGit until the
  next login.

Upgrade
  Replace OwnGit.app with the new version and open it. The app restarts the
  service with its new program. Replacing the app does not remove state or
  repositories. An older app is not promised to read state after a completed
  schema migration.

Remove
  Run {{.Helper}} service uninstall first, then quit
  the icon and move OwnGit.app to Trash. The service would otherwise keep
  trying to start a program that is gone. State and repositories are
  retained.

Requirements
  Git must already be installed. Pull request merge requires Git 2.38 or newer.

Coding tool integration
  OwnGit.app/Contents/Resources/docs/CODING_TOOLS.md
  OwnGit.app/Contents/Resources/docs/CODING_TOOLS.ko.md (the guide in Korean)
  OwnGit.app/Contents/Resources/integrations/skills/owngit-checks/SKILL.md
  Copy the skill yourself, or run owngit skill --install DIR, if you want a
  coding tool to load it. The helper binary is at
  {{.Helper}} and is not on PATH.

Public readiness
{{- if .Signed}}
  Public distribution additionally requires observed Gatekeeper behavior on a
  Mac that did not build it and a completed native acceptance run.
{{- else}}
  Public distribution additionally requires an authorized Developer ID
  signature, hardened runtime, notarization, stapling, and observed Gatekeeper
  behavior. No protection should be bypassed to run this prototype.
{{- end}}
